.TH RAISA 1 2026-11-10 "raisa 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
raisa \- terminal client for the SCP Wiki
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raisa
.RB [ \-b
.IR branch ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raisa
reads the SCP Wiki in a terminal. The screen shows the bookmarks on the left
(as wide as the longest title, at most 0.3 of the window; longer titles wrap)
and the open page on the right: an article, a series list or a hub, the text
centred and up to 80 characters wide. The column that is not focused is dim; a
narrow window shows only the focused one. Back and forward work like in a
browser. The main page of the site starts with the site menu (series, hubs,
tales and so on).
.PP
The top line shows "SCP Foundation - en" (the branch code); on the right,
messages, loading, the address of the selected link or of the open page. On an
object page its background shows the object class in the terminal colours: Safe
green, Euclid yellow, Keter red, Thaumiel magenta.
.PP
Images are drawn in the text when python-pillow is installed (SVG also needs
rsvg-convert from librsvg): with Sixel if the terminal supports it (foot does),
otherwise with half-block characters in 24-bit colour. A photo is as wide as the
text and at most two thirds of the screen high; icons, logos and buttons keep
their size.
.PP
One run reads one branch; links to other branches open in the web browser.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " branch"
The branch to read:
en cn cs de es fr it jp ko pl pt ru th ua vn zh int.
Default: en.
.TP
.I target
A page to open: 173, scp-682-j, 001-jp, a page name or a URL. Without it the
last page of the branch is opened with the reading position; on the first run,
the main page.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B j/k, arrow keys
scroll by a line
.TP
.B d/u, ^d/^u, PgDn/PgUp
scroll by half a screen
.TP
.B Space
scroll by a whole screen
.TP
.B g/G, Home/End
go to the top or the bottom
.TP
.B n, p/N
go to the next or the previous page or position
.TP
.B J/K
select the next or the previous link
.TP
.B Tab/Shift-Tab, h/l
switch between the bookmarks and the text
.TP
.B Enter
open the selected link or bookmark
.TP
.B Esc
close the search
.TP
.B /
search the site
.TP
.B m
open the main page of the site
.TP
.B o
open the current page in the browser
.TP
.B i
open the image in an external viewer
.TP
.B b
bookmark the current page, or remove the bookmark
.TP
.B B
bookmark the selected link, or remove the bookmark
.TP
.B x
remove the selected bookmark
.TP
.B q
quit
.PP
A jump with g or G is a step like following a link: N returns from it.
.PP
A bookmark is titled as the page calls itself: on most branches an object page
is titled with its number alone, on some (the Russian one) with its name too. So
B loads the page before bookmarking it.
.PP
The bookmarks column lists the bookmarks of the current branch, alphabetically.
While it is focused, the keys that scroll move its cursor (J/K too).
.SS Search
The search line opens at the bottom. Enter on an object number or a URL goes
there; Enter on words opens a page of results, read and followed like any page:
under Titles, pages whose title matches (the Crom index, at most five); on the
Russian branch also under Text, the site's full-text search with excerpts, ten
a page, then a More results link. Esc, or Backspace on an empty line, closes the
line. Pasting text opens the line with that text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/raisa/
pages (fresh for a day), images,
the Anubis cookie pass
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/raisa/state.json
bookmarks and the last page of every branch
.SH NOTES
Several copies can run at once, for example one per branch in two windows: every
change to state.json re-reads it under a lock, so no bookmark is lost.
.PP
If something goes wrong, a message appears in the top line, and the details are
printed to the terminal after exit.
.PP
In a terminal with the kitty keyboard protocol (foot, kitty, WezTerm, Ghostty,
Alacritty) raisa turns it on by itself, so hotkeys work in any keyboard layout.
Other terminals (xterm, cool-retro-term, the Linux console) work too; there
hotkeys work in the US and Russian layouts.
.PP
The Russian site is protected by Anubis; raisa solves its check like a browser
does. The check is tied to the IP address, so it fails when the outgoing address
changes between requests (some VPNs). Title search uses the Crom index
(api.crom.avn.sh). Full-text search exists only on the Russian branch:
Wikidot's own search is turned off.
